{
  "about": "Which prop art (manifest.json in this folder) dresses each thing in data/locations, read by world/look/set_dressing.gd (docs/art/set_dressing.md). A location prop or container is looked up by its id in `ids` first, then by its `model` in `models`; with neither it uses the art of the same name as its model, else `container_default` for containers. A value is an art id, or {art, mount, scale} to override how it hangs, or null for an invisible spot (something already drawn, or a view). `on_wall` is the art used when the thing stands on a wall square (shelves against a wall). Doors take the first `doors.rules` entry whose words are in their id or label. `floors` gives a place its own ground texture; `low_cover.<place>` and `<place>_run` dress its '=' squares. An entry with `building: true` stands in for the whole house on its square (a windmill, a bell tower); `fade: true` fades a tall piece like the trees. `scales` sizes a piece wherever it stands (stairs fill their square); `fronts` gives furniture a front view that stands flat against a wall beside it. `rooms` gives a location's areas their own floor and wall by words in the area's name (a bathroom's tiles); `place_looks` overrides a whole place's floor, wall, difficult ground and `rock_walls` (cliffs instead of trees).",
  "container_default": "chest",
